    "==================================================================================\nIMPORTANT NOTICE\n==================================================================================\nBefore you can access and play our game, you must accept the following legal documents (full texts are available below after this notice):\n\n* End User License Agreement - outlines the license terms, limitations, restrictions, termination, and rules of conduct in our game.\n\n* Privacy Policy - explains how we handle and protect your personal data when you interact with our games and services.\n\nPlease take a moment to read these documents carefully before accepting them. If you disagree with any of them, you cannot use our game or any other related services.\n==================================================================================\nEND USER LICENSE AGREEMENT\n==================================================================================\n\nPublished: April 29, 2026\n\nTHIS END USER LICENSE AGREEMENT (\"AGREEMENT\") IS A LEGALLY BINDING CONTRACT BETWEEN YOU (\"USER\") AND PIXEL TECHNOLOGIES - FZCO (\"PUBLISHER\"), A COMPANY REGISTERED AND OPERATING UNDER THE LAWS OF THE UNITED ARAB EMIRATES (REGISTRATION NUMBER: DSO-FZCO-24339). THIS AGREEMENT SPECIFIES THE TERMS OF USE FOR THE ONLINE FREE MULTIPLAYER GAMES PROVIDED BY THE PUBLISHER AS A REGIONAL DISTRIBUTOR, INCLUDING BUT NOT LIMITED TO WAR THUNDER, CROSSOUT AND ENLISTED VIDEOGAMES (COLLECTIVELY – \"GAME\").\n\nPLEASE READ THIS AGREEMENT CAREFULLY. BY DOWNLOADING, INSTALLING, OR LAUNCHING THE GAME, AS WELL AS PURCHASING IN-GAME GOODS AND SERVICES, YOU ACCEPT THE TERMS OF THIS AGREEMENT, THE PUBLISHER’S PRIVACY POLICY AVAILABLE AT HTTPS://PIXELTECHNOLOGIES.IO/PRIVACYPOLICY, AND ANY APPLICABLE GAME-RELATED RULES AND POLICIES. IF YOU DO NOT AGREE TO THESE TERMS, THE PRIVACY POLICY, OR THE RELATED RULES AND DOCUMENTS, YOU ARE NOT PERMITTED TO USE THE GAME.\n\nTHIS AGREEMENT APPLIES TO ALL VERSIONS OF THE GAME IN THE VERSION USED BY THE USER, INCLUDING ALL FUTURE VERSIONS AND UPDATES, UNLESS A SEPARATE AGREEMENT IS REQUIRED TO USE SUCH A VERSION.\n\nUNLESS STATED OTHERWISE, ALL TERMS MENTIONED IN THE SINGULAR FORM IN THIS AGREEMENT APPLY TO THE SAME TERMS IN THE PLURAL FORM, AND VICE VERSA.\n\n1. GAME ACCESS RULES\n\n1.1. You may become a User if you are at least 18 years old, or the minimum age required by the laws of your country of residence, at the time you accept this Agreement. You must also have a valid account that allows you to access the Game, use it, and store information such as in-game items, currency, and other data (\"Account\"). Third-party platforms involved in the Game distribution may have specific rules for creating, using, and deleting an Account specified in their legal documents.\n1.2. The Game is not intended for use by individuals whose participation in the Game is prohibited or restricted by applicable law or this Agreement. Additionally, the Game is not intended for use by individuals whose Accounts have been blocked, deleted, or disabled for any reason. Using the Game in violation of these restrictions may result in blocking access to the Game or deletion/suspending of the Account.\n1.3. If the User is a minor according to the laws of their country of residence, they must obtain the consent of their parents or guardians to use the Game and to accept this Agreement, the privacy policy, and other applicable rules and policies.\n1.4. The Game may contain links to third-party websites, services, or resources not controlled or endorsed by the Publisher. You agree that the Publisher is not responsible for the availability, content, or accuracy of such sites, services, or resources. Use of these services or resources is at your own risk.\n1.5. Users are responsible for keeping their Account credentials confidential and preventing unauthorized access. Any actions taken in the Game under your Account are considered to be done by you. The User is solely responsible for all activities on their Account, whether authorized or not.\n\n2. LIMITED LICENSE\n\n2.1. Provided that you comply with the provisions of this Agreement, the Publisher grants you a non-exclusive, non-transferable, non-sublicensable, limited license to access and use the Game and its additional functionality (see Section 3 of this Agreement) solely for personal, non-commercial purposes, in the following ways:\n2.1.1. Participate in the Game and modify the content of the Game during such participation in compliance with the Game Rules;\n2.1.2. Reproduce the client part of the Game by installing it on your personal computer for the purpose of participating in the Game;\n2.1.3. Use the additional functionality of the Game (Non-activated Data and Commands) in accordance with this Agreement, provided that you pay for the corresponding right;\n2.1.4. Use the Game only within the framework of its normal functioning, without exceeding the limits set by the developer or the basic game mechanics. \"Normal functioning \" means operating the Game based on its client part as intended by the developer or basic game mechanics.\n2.2. You are prohibited from:\n2.2.1. Copying, modifying, distributing, selling, leasing, sublicensing, or otherwise transferring the Game or its elements;\n2.2.2. Using the Game or its parts to create derivative works;\n2.2.3. Decompiling, reverse engineering, or otherwise extracting the source code of the Game;\n2.2.4. Deleting, modifying, or concealing any copyright notices, trademarks, or other legal notices contained in the Game;\n2.2.5. Using the Game for any illegal or prohibited purposes, including:\n•\tEmploying cheat programs, bots, modifications, hacks, trainers, automated programs, scripts, or any other third-party software intended to alter gameplay, bypass technical protection measures, gain unauthorized access to the Game's functionality, automate game processes, or gain an advantage over other players;\n•\tExploiting software bugs or vulnerabilities in the Game for personal gain or sharing such information with third parties;\n•\tPerforming actions aimed at disrupting the stable operation of the Game, its servers, or network infrastructure;\n•\tGaining unauthorized access to other users' accounts or attempting to obtain such data.\n2.3. You agree that the Publisher does not transfer any intellectual property or other proprietary rights to you regarding the Game, except for the limited license granted in this section.\n2.4. The Publisher reserves the right, at its sole discretion and without prior notice, to suspend or revoke the license granted to you to use the Game or its elements at any time and for any reason, including violations of this Agreement or any applicable laws.\n2.5. In the event of termination of this Agreement for any reason, all limited licenses and rights granted to you to use the Game—including Non-activated Data and Commands (as defined in Section 3 below)—will also terminate, regardless of the platform or provider from which they were acquired. Under no circumstances is the Publisher obligated to provide compensation or refunds for funds paid for non-activated elements of the Game.\n2.6. The Publisher reserves the right to determine the territory within which the rights to use the Game are granted under this Agreement. \nUnless explicitly specified otherwise by the Publisher for a specific Game, the territory includes Azerbaijan, Armenia, Belarus, Georgia, Kazakhstan, Kyrgyzstan, Moldova, Russia, Tajikistan, Turkmenistan, and Uzbekistan.\n2.7. When using the Game, you are required to comply with the Game Rules outlined in Annex No. 1 of this Agreement.\n2.8. The User acknowledges and agrees that the computer code, audiovisual elements, visual images, sounds, music, text, game mechanics, characters, items, systems, methods of operation, documentation, and other materials and components incorporated into or made available through the Game are protected by intellectual property laws and may constitute valuable intellectual property, confidential information, and/or trade secrets of the relevant right holder(s), including the developer, licensors, suppliers, and other authorized parties. The Game distributed by the Publisher is based on intellectual property owned, licensed, or otherwise controlled by the relevant right holder(s), and the Publisher distributes such Game and protects the related rights within its authorized territory. Nothing in this Agreement shall be construed as granting the User any ownership rights in or to the Game or any of its elements, except for the limited rights expressly granted under this Agreement.  The User further acknowledges that the Game is a commercial digital product, the operation, availability, composition, content, and technical architecture of which may be determined, modified, restricted, suspended, or discontinued by the Publisher and/or the relevant right holder(s) in their discretion, subject to applicable law. In order to protect the Game, its lawful operation, the gameplay environment, the rights and legitimate interests of the Publisher, the developer, and the relevant right holder(s), as well as to prevent cheating, circumvention, unauthorized use, unlawful copying, unauthorized access, and other violations, the Publisher, the developer, and/or their authorized contractors and service providers may apply various technical protection measures, control technologies, validation mechanisms, digital rights management tools, anti-cheat technologies, security monitoring solutions, and other technical means.  By installing, accessing, or using the Game, the User acknowledges and agrees to the use and operation of such technical measures to the extent necessary for the above purposes, including for verifying the legitimacy of access to the Game, detecting prohibited software, preventing unfair play, enforcing this Agreement and the Game Rules, protecting the intellectual property and related rights embodied in the Game, and maintaining the security, integrity, and proper functioning of the Game and its infrastructure. Any attempt to bypass, disable, interfere with, manipulate, or otherwise undermine such technical measures shall constitute a material breach of this Agreement and may result in suspension or termination of access to the Game, without prejudice to any other rights or remedies available to the Publisher and/or the relevant right holder(s).\n\n3. TERMS OF USE FOR NON-ACTIVATED DATA AND COMMANDS\n\n3.1. The Game may offer additional paid functionality—such as in-game items, in-game currency, premium accounts, and others—that simplifies gameplay by providing additional advantages, elements, and capabilities and also expands the Game's functionality (the \"Non-activated Data and Commands\"). The purchase and payment for the rights to use the Non-activated Data and Commands are not necessary conditions for participating in the Game or obtaining the rights to use the Game as a whole. The rights to use the Non-activated Data and Commands are provided at your request and discretion. The Non-activated Data and Commands are integral part of the Game, are not a separate computer program, and the rights to its use can be exercised by you only in connection with the use of the Game. Rights to Non-activated Data and Commands are available for use exclusively within the Game and cannot be transferred or sold outside the Game.\n3.2. Users may acquire Non-activated Data and Commands from the Publisher directly or through digital distribution platforms, partner services, app stores, and other third-party distribution channels authorized by the Publisher, including, where applicable, the Apple App Store, Google Play, Huawei AppGallery, and any other official distribution partners recognized by the Publisher in its sole discretion. In some cases, certain parts of the Game may be available free of charge, while access to certain features of the Game or certain Non-activated Data and Commands may require payment.\nIf you purchase paid Non-activated Data and Commands, you must complete such purchase only through the payment methods, platforms, and service providers made available, recognized, or otherwise authorized by the Publisher. You agree to provide current, complete, and accurate payment information to such third-party platforms and providers. When making a payment through third-party payment providers, app stores, or distribution partners, your payment will also be subject to their applicable terms and conditions, privacy policies, and refund policies, which you must review before completing the purchase. You are solely responsible for all activity conducted through your Account, including all fees, taxes, charges, and other amounts incurred through or in connection with your Account.\n3.3. You agree that the Publisher has the right to change the terms and conditions for providing Non-activated Data and Commands.\n3.4. In some Games, in-game currency may be awarded to the User without a fee for performing specific actions within the Game (for example, reaching a new level or completing Game tasks).\n3.5. You agree to use the Non-activated Data and Commands only in accordance with this Agreement and applicable law. You may not sell, transfer, exchange, or use the Non-activated Data and Commands for illegal or prohibited purposes.\n3.6. You may purchase Non-activated Data and Commands using real money and/or other payment methods, where such methods are supported by the relevant Game, platform, or authorized payment provider. Once the Publisher or the applicable authorized third-party platform receives confirmation of payment, the relevant Non-activated Data and Commands shall be deemed purchased. The Publisher reserves the right, at its sole discretion, to change, modify, suspend, discontinue, or remove any aspect of the Non-activated Data and Commands, including their availability or price.\nAll sales of Non-activated Data and Commands are final, and no refunds, exchanges, or transfers will be provided except as required by applicable law or by the mandatory rules of the relevant third-party platform through which the purchase was made. If the purchase was made through the Apple App Store, Google Play, Huawei AppGallery, or another authorized third-party distribution partner, the applicable refund and payment rules of such platform or partner may apply. The Publisher may, but is not obligated to, assist the User in communicating with the relevant platform regarding a refund request, but the decision on such refund remains with the applicable platform to the extent required by its rules or applicable law.\n3.7. The price of some Non-activated Data and Commands, including in-game items, may be indicated in virtual in-game currency. Please note that such virtual currency, consisting of software code and audiovisual elements integrated into the Game, does not constitute real money. The Publisher sets the exchange rate between virtual and real currency, displayed in the in-game store. Please note that the store is a feature of the Game and is not intended for financial trading.\n3.8. Non-activated Data and Commands may have an expiration date or other restrictions the Publisher sets. If not used within a specified period, they may be canceled without notice and without compensation.\n3.9. The Publisher reserves the right to change or remove any rights to Non-activated Data and Commands from the Game at its discretion without prior notice. In the event of termination or modification of the rights to Non-activated Data and Commands for any reason, the Publisher does not provide refunds or compensation for the respective rights to Non-activated Data and Commands, as specified in clause 8.1 of the Agreement below.\n3.10. You agree that the Publisher does not guarantee the following:\n3.10.1. Desired in-game items will be available when in-game currency is credited to the User's Account.\n3.10.2. You can use the Non-activated Data and Commands for an indefinite or desired period.\n3.10.3. You can exchange Non-activated Data and Commands for any specific in-game items or functions.\n3.10.4. The characteristics or intended use of the Non-activated Data and Commands will remain unchanged throughout the use of the Game or will meet your expectations and preferences.\n3.11. You agree that the Publisher does not exchange purchased Non-activated Data and Commands (for example, in-game currency or in-game items) for cash or non-cash items, does not compensate your expenses, in particular, for any User transactions, and does not pay interest on the use of funds, as Non-activated Data and Commands are an additional feature of the Game, and their payment is a fee for a license to use extended Game functionality. You are not allowed to purchase Non-activated Data and Commands (for example, in-game currency) from third parties not authorized by the Publisher.\n3.12. Only the Publisher and authorized persons can provide all Non-activated Data and Commands. If a User accesses paid features from unauthorized third parties, the Publisher can block their access, fix any issues caused by using these features, and end the Agreement with the User.\n3.13. When a User obtains Non-activated Data and Commands due to a technical error, malfunction, incomplete payment, or without using in-game currency, the Publisher can deduct the cost from future payments or block (restrict) the User's Account.\n3.14. The User shall bear all costs associated with transferring funds when purchasing rights to Non-activated Data and Commands, including any fees. The User must keep all documents confirming the payment of rights to Non-activated Data and Commands for their participation in the Game and provide them to the Publisher upon request.\n3.15. The Publisher reserves the right to unilaterally modify the terms of access to the Game (including paid features) at any time or to discontinue support for the Game partially or fully. These changes can alter or end this Agreement without the User's consent.\n3.16. The Publisher may use third parties, including intermediaries and payment systems, to facilitate transactions or provide rights to Non-activated Data and Commands without the User's approval. It is the User's responsibility to understand and accept these third parties' terms before making payments.\n3.17. Terms of Use for Subscriptions  \n3.17.1. Certain products, features, or additional functionality available within the Game may be offered on a recurring subscription basis with automatic billing at fixed intervals (“Subscription”). By purchasing a Subscription, the User acknowledges and agrees that Subscription fees will be charged automatically on a recurring basis until the Subscription is cancelled in accordance with this Agreement and, where applicable, the rules of the relevant third-party platform through which the Subscription was purchased.  \n3.17.2. The material terms of the Subscription, including its initial period, renewal period, billing frequency, price, scope of benefits, and other relevant information, will be presented to the User in the applicable Subscription purchase interface before the Subscription is confirmed.  \n3.17.3. The Publisher reserves the right to change the price of any Subscription at any time. If the Publisher changes the price of a Subscription, the User will be notified in advance no later than 30 calendar days before such change takes effect, unless a shorter period is permitted or required by applicable law or unless different rules apply under the terms of the relevant third-party platform through which the Subscription was purchased.  \n3.17.4. The User may cancel a Subscription at any time. Unless otherwise required by the applicable platform or by applicable law, such cancellation will take effect at the beginning of the next billing cycle, and the User will continue to have access to the Subscription benefits until the end of the then-current paid Subscription period.  \n3.17.5. If a Subscription payment cannot be processed due to an issue with the User’s selected payment method, the Publisher or the relevant third-party platform may suspend, restrict, or terminate the Subscription until payment is successfully processed. This may affect the start of the next Subscription period and the billing date for subsequent periods. If the applicable payment method cannot be charged, including due to expiration, invalidity, insufficient funds, or other payment failure, the User remains responsible for any outstanding amounts to the extent permitted by applicable law and the applicable rules of the relevant platform.  \n3.17.6. The Publisher reserves the right to suspend or terminate the User’s Subscription at any time, including immediately, if: (a) the User fails to pay the applicable Subscription fee; (b) the User violates this Agreement, the Game Rules, or other applicable rules or policies; (c) the User’s Account is suspended, restricted, or terminated; or (d) the Publisher discontinues or materially changes the relevant Subscription, related functionality, or the Game. In the event of suspension, restriction, or termination of the User’s access to the Game or Account due to the User’s violation of this Agreement or other applicable rules, the User shall not be entitled to any refund, compensation, or credit for any unused portion of the Subscription, except where required by applicable law.\n\n4. GAME USAGE RESTRICTIONS\n\n4.1. In addition to other restrictions on the use of the Game provided in this Agreement, the User agrees not to perform the following actions:\n4.1.1. Use the Game to transmit unauthorized information, including but not limited to unsolicited emails, spam, and any materials promoting malicious or spyware software, as well as uploading files with false or harmful content.\n4.1.2. Harvest (mass collect) or otherwise obtain any Game data that is not intended to be displayed during the normal functioning of the Game (as intended by the developer).\n4.1.3. Facilitate, create, or maintain any unauthorized connections to the Game, including connections to unauthorized servers that emulate or attempt to emulate the Game's servers.\n4.1.4. Post offensive, threatening, obscene, defamatory information, as well as materials containing racial, sexual, religious, or other discrimination, and distribute links to such information.\n4.1.5. Insult or otherwise violate the rights of other Users.\n4.2. The Publisher may offer the User participation in beta testing of the Game or its components. The User acknowledges that the beta version of the Game may contain errors, malfunctions, and may not provide stable operation. If the User agrees to participate in beta testing, the User agrees to:\n4.2.1. Report to the Publisher any detected errors, problems, and suggestions for improving the Game.\n4.2.2. Comply with all additional terms and restrictions established by the Publisher for beta testing.\n\n5. USER CONTENT\n\n5.1. The Game may provide Users with the ability to create, upload, send, transmit, or otherwise make available within the Game various materials, such as texts, images, videos, audio files, and other forms of content (\"User Content\").\n5.2. You are solely responsible for all User Content that you publish, and for any consequences of its publication or use. The Publisher is not responsible for User Content or any claims, damages, or losses resulting from its use.\n5.3. You retain all rights to the User Content you publish. However, by providing User Content through the Games, you grant the Publisher a non-exclusive, perpetual, royalty-free, transferable, sublicensable, worldwide license to use, copy, modify, create derivative works from, publish, display, perform, transmit, and distribute such User Content in connection with the distribution of the Game and the development of related products and services.\n5.4. You agree not to create, upload, send, or make available User Content through the Game if such content:\n5.4.1. Is illegal, threatening, abusive, discriminatory, pornographic, defamatory, harmful, invasive of privacy, or contrary to moral and ethical norms.\n5.4.2. Infringes copyrights, patents, trademarks, trade secrets, or other intellectual property rights.\n5.4.3. Contains viruses, worms, Trojan horses, or other harmful code.\n5.4.4. Violates this Agreement or any applicable laws.\n5.5. The Publisher does not guarantee the accuracy, quality, or completeness of any User Content posted in the Game. By using the Game, you agree that you may encounter materials that may be offensive. You also agree that the Publisher is not responsible for User Content under any circumstances.\n5.6. The Publisher has the right to remove, temporarily or permanently, any User Content from the Game without notice to the User who posted such User Content.\n\n6. LIMITATION OF LIABILITY AND DISCLAIMER OF WARRANTIES\n\n6.1. The Games are provided \"as is\" and \"as available\", and you acknowledge that:\n6.1.1. The Game may not meet your requirements.\n6.1.2. Access to the Game may not be uninterrupted, timely, secure, or error-free.\n6.1.3. The results obtained from using the Game may not be accurate or reliable.\n6.1.4. The quality of any products, services, information, or other material purchased or obtained by you through the Game may not meet your expectations.\n6.1.5. Any errors in the Game software will not necessarily be corrected.\n6.2. The Publisher is not liable for:\n6.2.1. Any lack of User access to the internet, the quality of internet service providers, or any difficulties or inability to use the Game due to these circumstances.\n6.2.2. Any losses incurred by the User during access to the Game, including losses caused by errors, interruptions, file deletions, functionality changes, defects, delays in data transmission, or other occurrences not caused by the Publisher.\n6.2.3. Any loss or damage arising from the use, non-use, or inability to use the Non-activated Data and Commands.\n6.2.4. Damage to the User or third parties, including damage resulting from the use or inability to use the Games, unauthorized access to a User's personal information, or the User's Account.\n6.3. The Publisher's liability to the User is limited to the amount paid by the User for purchasing the Non-activated Data and Commands unless otherwise provided by applicable law.\n6.4. The Publisher is not required to provide any evidence of the User's breach of the Agreement that resulted in the termination of this Agreement.\n6.5. You agree that the Game may contain audio and/or visual effects that may provoke epileptic or other nervous system disorders, and you warrant that you do not suffer from such disorders or will not use the Game in such cases.\n6.6. The Publisher provides technical support related to the use of the Game through third-party platforms (game distribution services, online stores, and similar platforms). For necessary technical support, Users should directly contact the support service of the respective third-party platforms, specifying the game released by the Publisher. Users must provide all the required information related to their request to ensure timely and effective resolution of any issues or problems. The Publisher makes every effort to cooperate with third-party platforms to provide quality technical support for Users but is not responsible for the actions or inactions of third parties in the support process.\n\n7. TERMINATION AND SUSPENSION OF THE AGREEMENT\n\n7.1. This Agreement becomes effective when the User first downloads, installs, or otherwise uses the Game (including by purchasing the Non-activated Data and Commands) and remains in effect until terminated as provided below.\n7.2. Unless otherwise required by law, the Publisher may unilaterally terminate this Agreement at any time without notice to the User and without any obligation to compensate the User for any costs or amounts.\n7.3. If a User violates the terms of this Agreement, access to the Game may be immediately and without warning denied or restricted. The grounds for such denial or restriction of access may be provided in the Game Rules.\n7.4. The Publisher reserves the right to unilaterally suspend or terminate the Game’s functionality if it suspects the User of illegal activities until all circumstances are clarified. In certain situations, the Publisher may also pass information about the User who violates the terms of the Agreement or applicable law to law enforcement authorities.\n7.5. The User acknowledges and agrees that the Games are distributed by the Publisher on various distribution platforms, online stores, and other services (collectively referred to as \"Platforms\") at the Publisher's discretion. In this regard:\n7.5.1. Any violations of this Agreement (including license restrictions and Game Rules) may result in blocking, restricting access, or other sanctions by the respective Platform. In particular, due to in-game violations, your account on the respective Platform may be blocked or restricted, or you may lose the ability to play the Game through that Platform.\n7.5.2. Any violations of the terms of use of the Platforms constitute a breach of this Agreement. Please note that in case you violate such terms, you may lose the ability to use the Games.\n7.5.3. The User acknowledges and agrees that in the event of blocking, restricting access, or other sanctions by the Publisher or the Platforms related to the User's violation of this Agreement or the terms of use of the Platforms, the Publisher has no obligation to provide any compensation or refunds, including but not limited to funds paid for Non-activated Data and Commands and any Subscription.\n7.5.4. The User may terminate this Agreement at any time by deleting the Game or their Account on the respective Platform (if applicable). However, deleting the Game or Account does not release the User from obligations arising prior to the termination of the Agreement, including but not limited to obligations to compensate for damages caused to the Publisher as a result of the User's violation of the terms of this Agreement.\n\n8. FINAL PROVISIONS\n\n8.1.  The User agrees that the Game may periodically update automatically without prior notice or consent. The Publisher reserves the right, at any time and at its sole discretion, to make changes, updates, or additions to the Game—including adjustments to game balance, functionality (including Non-activated Data and Commands), user interface, or content—to enhance the gameplay experience for Users. The Publisher may also close or limit the Game's functionality without prior notice.\nThe User acknowledges and agrees that in the event of any such changes, updates, limitations, or if the Game or any of its components are discontinued, the Publisher is not obligated to provide any compensation or refunds, including those for funds paid for Non-activated Data and Commands or any Subscription.\n8.2. The User acknowledges that all exclusive rights to the Games, including game characters, items and accessories, game coins, in-game values, graphics, photographs, animations, video images, video clips, sound recordings, sound effects, music, text content of the Game, and other components, belong to the respective right holders. The User understands that each element of the Game, including game characters, is part of computer software and is protected by copyright. While using the Game, Users may control game characters, including their development, but such control and development do not imply the transfer of exclusive rights from the Publisher to the User. Control and development of characters cannot be considered as the User’s authorship or co-authorship in relation to game characters and/or co-authorship with the game right holder.\n8.3. The User cannot assign their rights and obligations under this Agreement to third parties, either for a fee or free of charge.\n8.4. The Publisher can change this Agreement without notifying the User. Changes are effective immediately once published in the Game, on the Publisher's website, or on the Game distribution site. The User must regularly review the Agreement for any changes. Users must fulfill their obligations and comply with the Agreement’s rules, regardless of whether they know about any changes.\n8.5. If a court declares any provision of this Agreement invalid, the rest of the Agreement remains in effect. In this situation, the parties are required to follow the remaining valid provisions and attempt to fulfill the initial intentions of the Agreement as closely as possible.\n8.6. All disputes arising from this Agreement or in connection with it, including those related to its conclusion, execution, interpretation, cancellation, termination, or invalidity, as well as any other disputes arising from this Agreement or related to it, shall be resolved through arbitration in accordance with the rules of the Dubai International Arbitration Centre (DIAC) by a single arbitrator appointed in accordance with these rules. The arbitration will take place in Dubai, UAE. The law of England and Wales, without regard to its conflict of laws principles, shall apply to all matters arising from or related to this Agreement.\n8.7. Should this Agreement or any related documents be translated into other languages, and a discrepancy arises between the versions, the English language version shall prevail.\n8.8. Additional Terms for Apple App Store.  If the Game is accessed, downloaded, installed, purchased, or used on any device manufactured by Apple Inc. or through the Apple App Store, the following additional terms shall apply:  this Agreement is concluded solely between the User and the Publisher, and not with Apple Inc. (“Apple”). Apple is not responsible for the Game, its content, operation, maintenance, support, or any claims relating to the Game. The use of the Game on Apple-branded devices is additionally subject to the applicable Apple Media Services Terms and Conditions and related Apple usage rules, which shall prevail to the extent required by such rules.  The license granted under this Agreement is non-transferable and is limited to the right to use the Game on Apple-branded products that the User owns or controls, and as otherwise permitted by the applicable Apple usage rules, including via Family Sharing, volume purchasing, or other lawful arrangements recognized by Apple. Apple has no obligation whatsoever to provide maintenance or support services with respect to the Game.  The Publisher, acting as regional distributor of the Game based on intellectual property owned, licensed, or otherwise controlled by the relevant right holder(s), remains solely responsible for any warranties relating to the Game, to the extent such warranties cannot be disclaimed under applicable law, and for addressing any claims by the User or any third party relating to the Game, including product liability claims, claims that the Game fails to conform to applicable legal or regulatory requirements, claims arising under consumer protection or similar legislation, and claims alleging infringement of third-party intellectual property rights. To the extent the Game fails to conform to any applicable warranty that cannot lawfully be disclaimed, the User may notify Apple, and Apple may refund the purchase price paid for the Game, if any, in accordance with Apple’s applicable rules; to the maximum extent permitted by applicable law, Apple shall have no other warranty obligation whatsoever with respect to the Game.  The User represents and warrants that the User is not located in a country or territory subject to a U.S. government embargo, and is not included on any U.S. government list of prohibited or restricted parties, including the U.S. Treasury Department’s list of Specially Designated Nationals and Blocked Persons, the U.S. Department of Commerce Denied Persons List, or the Entity List.  The User agrees that, except as expressly set out herein, this Agreement does not create rights in favor of any third party. Notwithstanding the foregoing, Apple and Apple’s subsidiaries shall be deemed third-party beneficiaries of this Agreement solely to the extent required under the applicable Apple rules, and, upon the User’s acceptance of this Agreement, Apple shall have the right to enforce this Agreement against the User as such third-party beneficiary.\n\nANNEX NO. 1. GAME RULES\n\nTHE USER MUST FOLLOW THE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFIED IN THE DEVELOPER'S GAME RULES, AVAILABLE AT HTTPS://LEGAL.GAIJIN.NET/RU/TERMSOFSERVICE. THE USER ACKNOWLEDGES THAT THESE RULES MAY BE UPDATED, AND SUCH UPDATES AUTOMATICALLY APPLY TO GAMES PROVIDED BY PIXEL TECHNOLOGIES - FZCO (\"PUBLISHER\"), A COMPANY, REGISTERED AND OPERATING UNDER THE LAWS OF THE UNITED ARAB EMIRATES (REGISTRATION NUMBER: DSO-FZCO-24339) (\"ADMINISTRATION\"). IT IS THE USER'S RESPONSIBILITY TO REGULARLY CHECK THE DEVELOPER'S WEBSITE FOR THE CURRENT VERSION OF THESE RULES.\n\n1. To ensure an enjoyable gaming experience for everybody, you must behave respectfully and appropriately towards other players while playing our Games. This includes, without limitation, that you are not allowed to use nicknames or clan (squadron, etc.) names, slogans, logos, descriptions, etc., or disseminate other content that is unlawful, sexually related, misleading, misrepresentative, or promotes hate speech, contains derogatory, offensive remarks, or that relates to controversial figures or groups in a way that incites conflict, degrades human dignity, or encourages forceful governmental overthrow.\n2. You must play fair and not intentionally disrupt your team's gameplay. For example, you must not hurt your teammates on purpose (\"friendly fire\"), block their movements, or stay inactive (\"AFK\") during a game session. You must not use cheats, bugs, exploits, or other methods of unfair play.\n3. You must not share spam, use offensive language, promote discrimination, post provocative content, engage in discussions violating the law, spread hate speech or endorse other harmful propaganda, or discuss matters that breach decency and morality, whether in text- or voice-based chats, or otherwise. You must also not share other individuals’ personal data, threaten, disseminate false information, or publicly discuss the Administration's actions. You must use the language proper to the game chat’s language zone (if any).\n4. You may not use the in-game complaint system to send irrelevant or groundless complaints or insult any person, whether individual, group, or corporate.\n5. Users may report objectionable content they have encountered in the game chats. We usually review such reports within two weeks and may take appropriate measures. However, we reserve the right not to disclose the details of our decision.\n6. We do not support or endorse political entities, and using our Games for any political purpose is prohibited. Among other things, messages in the game chats, clan (squadron, etc.) names, logos, and descriptions should not contain political content, except for the neutral content that Gaijin might occasionally add (for example, flags and national emblems of the United Nations Member States).\n7. Administration reserves the right not to interfere in the clan’s activities, especially in the distribution of clan authority between its members, actions of clan managers, or if someone creates a clan with a similar name or logo.\n8. If you violate these rules, the Administration may undertake any restorative measure or impose a penalty of their choice at any time and without further explanation, for example, by amending infringing nicknames or clan (squadron, etc.) names/descriptions, restricting your access to a Game, disbanding a clan (squadron, etc.), imposing restrictions on the use of game chats (\"mute\"), delete or suspend your Account, or impose any other sanction. You will not be entitled to a refund or any kind of compensation in such a case.\n9. If your actions do not explicitly violate the rules outlined in this document but lead to substantial complaints from other Users or harm the interests of third parties or Gaijin, the Administration reserves the right to apply the Game access restriction or delete your Account.\n10. As a rule, the Administration's decisions are final. Any appeals are proceeded at their discretion on a case-by-case basis.\nIMPORTANT: For detailed information on prohibited actions and the corresponding penalties within our games, please visit the developer's official site at legal.gaijin.net/ru/codeofconduct. Note that this document serves as guidance only and does not restrict the Administration's interpretation and application of the Game Rules.\n\n==================================================================================\nPRIVACY POLICY\n==================================================================================\n\nEffective Date: Published: April 29, 2026\n\nThis Privacy Policy (the “Policy”) explains how Pixel Technologies - FZCO (“Pixel”, “Company”, “we”, “us”, “our”) collects, uses, stores, shares, transfers, and otherwise processes personal data in connection with our mobile games, multiplayer online games, related in-game features, and any other games published, operated, or made available by us that link to or refer to this Policy (collectively, the “Games”).\n\nPixel Technologies - FZCO is a company incorporated and operating under the laws of the United Arab Emirates, with registration number DSO-FZCO-24339, licence number 26105, and registered address at Dubai Silicon Oasis, IFZA Business Park, DDP, Building A1, Premises 26105-001, Dubai, United Arab Emirates. Unless expressly stated otherwise in this Policy, Pixel acts as the controller of the personal data processed under this Policy in relation to the operation, administration, support, moderation, analytics, advertising, and security of the Games.\n\nThis Policy is intended to be interpreted in accordance with UAE Federal Decree-Law No. 45 of 2021 on the Protection of Personal Data and other applicable laws of the United Arab Emirates.\n\nBy downloading, installing, registering for, accessing, or using the Games, you acknowledge that you have read this Policy. Where required by applicable law, we will request your consent separately for specific processing activities.\n\n1. SCOPE OF THIS POLICY\n\nThis Policy applies to the personal data we process when you use the Games, including when you:\n•\tinstall or play our Games distributed through stores or distribution platforms such as the Apple App Store, Google Play, Huawei AppGallery, or other authorized third-party distributors; \n•\tcreate or use a player profile made available within a Game; \n•\tinteract with in-game social, multiplayer, guild, team, chat, matchmaking, ranking, reward, tournament, or similar features; \n•\tcontact us for customer support, moderation appeals, bug reporting, account assistance, or other Game-related enquiries; or \n•\totherwise interact with us in connection with the Games. \n\nThis Policy does not apply to the practices of third parties that act as separate controllers of your personal data, including app stores, payment providers, mobile platform operators, third-party account or single-sign-on providers, device manufacturers, social media platforms, or independent websites and services that are governed by their own privacy notices.\n\n2. PERSONAL DATA WE COLLECT\n\nThe categories of personal data we process depend on the Game you use, the features you engage with, the platform through which you access the Game, and the choices you make.\n\n2.1. Data you provide directly to us\n\nWhen you contact us or interact with the Games, you may provide us with:\n•\tyour nickname, display name, username, player tag, guild or clan name, profile text, avatar, and other profile content you choose to provide; \n•\tyour email address and other contact details when you contact support or otherwise communicate with us; \n•\tthe content of your support requests, emails, tickets, moderation appeals, bug reports, screenshots, attachments, feedback, and any other information you choose to submit; \n•\tcontent you create or share through the Games, including chat messages, reports, submissions, or other user-generated content made available through the relevant Game. \n\n2.2. Data collected automatically through the Games\n\nOur primary automatic data collection occurs through the Games, mobile SDKs, server-side systems, and related technical infrastructure.\n\nDepending on the Game and its functionality, we may automatically collect:\n•\tgameplay and account-linked data, such as character data, levels, progress, rewards, achievements, inventory, battle history, guild or team membership, rankings, match history, referrals, social interactions, settings, moderation status, sanctions, and timestamps relating to your use of the Games; \n•\tusage data, such as session duration, feature interaction, clicks, taps, views, frequency of play, retention events, participation in in-game events, progression points, and other gameplay-related behavioral data; \n•\tdevice and technical data, such as device model, operating system, OS version, screen resolution, memory and performance parameters, app version, build version, browser type where relevant, crash data, error logs, diagnostics, and unique device or installation identifiers; \n•\tconnection and network data, such as IP address, language, country or approximate region inferred from IP, time zone, mobile carrier or network type, and server-request metadata; \n•\tadvertising and attribution data, such as advertising identifiers, install attribution, ad impressions, ad clicks, ad campaign source, and related measurement data; \n•\tsecurity and integrity data, such as fraud indicators, unusual login or device patterns, abuse-prevention signals, ban or enforcement records, report history, and anti-cheat or anti-tampering telemetry where relevant to a specific Game or feature. \n\n2.3. Data received from third parties\n\nWe may receive personal data from third parties, including:\n•\tapp stores and platform operators, which may provide us with store IDs, transaction confirmations, subscription status, region or country information, refund status, entitlement information, and other data necessary to validate purchases and manage access to paid or reward-based features; \n•\tthird-party login or authentication providers, which may provide us with identifiers, email addresses, display names, profile images, and authentication confirmations or tokens necessary to authorize gameplay access; \n•\tpayment processors and commerce partners, which may provide us with transaction IDs, payment confirmations, item data, subscription status, approximate billing region, anti-fraud signals, and limited reconciliation data; \n•\tadvertising, attribution, and analytics partners, which may provide campaign attribution data, ad-performance data, aggregated audience data, fraud-prevention signals, and related mobile measurement data; \n•\tcommunity, event, or distribution partners, where a Game or feature is operated in cooperation with a third party; and \n•\tother users, for example where they report abuse, invite you, refer you, add you to a guild or team, or otherwise interact with you through multiplayer functionality. \n\n2.4. Use of third-party service providers for account and support services\n\nFor certain Games, some accounts, authentication, purchase-related account assistance, and user-support services may be provided to us by third-party service providers.\n\nWhere such services are used in connection with the Games, such third-party service providers may process personal data on our behalf as our processor or service provider, including for account registration and sign-in, authentication, account recovery, purchase-related account support, and the handling of gameplay-related or technical support requests. In such cases, we seek to ensure that such processing is carried out only on our documented instructions or otherwise as permitted by applicable law, only for the relevant and authorized purposes, only for the period necessary to provide the relevant services, and subject to appropriate contractual, technical, and organizational measures designed to protect personal data against unauthorized or unlawful processing, accidental loss, destruction, alteration, or disclosure.\n\nWe also seek to ensure, as appropriate and taking into account the nature of the relevant services and applicable law, that such service providers are subject to obligations concerning confidentiality, restricted access on a need-to-know basis, implementation of appropriate security measures, assistance with compliance and data-subject requests where relevant, return or deletion of personal data upon completion of the relevant services unless retention is required by law, and provision of information reasonably necessary to demonstrate compliance with applicable personal-data obligations.\n\n2.5. Sensitive data\n\nWe do not intentionally request or collect sensitive personal data unless such processing is strictly necessary, lawful, and proportionate for a specific purpose such as account protection, fraud prevention, dispute resolution, legal compliance, or another purpose permitted by applicable law. If such processing becomes necessary, we will provide any additional notice or obtain any consent required under applicable law.\n\n3. PURPOSES OF PROCESSING AND LAWFUL BASES\n\nWe process personal data only where we have a lawful basis to do so. Depending on the circumstances, our lawful bases may include your consent, the performance of a contract with you or steps taken at your request before entering into a contract, compliance with legal or regulatory obligations, protection of public interest, the establishment, exercise, or defense of legal claims, and other lawful bases permitted by applicable law.\n\n3.1. To provide and operate the Games\n\nWe process personal data to make the Games function properly and to provide the core features you request. This includes creating and maintaining your player profile within the Game, linking gameplay to a valid platform or distributor account where applicable, saving progress, synchronizing entitlements, enabling multiplayer, guild, ranking, reward, event, and social features, ensuring compatibility with your device, and delivering updates, patches, and operational support.\n\n3.2. To provide cross-play and access to shared global and regional game environments  \n\nWe process personal data as necessary to provide you with cross-play functionality and access to shared game environments, including where the Game is also published, distributed, operated, or made available by a global publisher and/or other regional publishers or partners. In particular, where this is necessary to enable your access to the relevant shared game ecosystem, personal data may be shared with, and received from, Gaijin Entertainment and its subsidiaries and/or affiliates, which may process personal data as independent controllers in relation to the operation of the shared global or regional game environment. Such sharing is limited to the minimum personal data necessary for the relevant purposes and directly related to gameplay, access to the shared game environment, and the operation, security, and integrity of the relevant Game features. This may include, for example, in-game identifiers, gameplay and progression data, matchmaking and ranking data, guild data, moderation and enforcement-related data, and technical or security-related information required to support common servers and infrastructure, multiplayer features, events, moderation, anti-cheat measures, fraud prevention, and the application of certain account restrictions or bans across the relevant game ecosystem. For more information about how Gaijin processes personal data in such cases, please refer to Gaijin’s privacy policy: https://legal.gaijin.net/privacypolicy.\n\n3.3. To authenticate access and maintain account integrity\n\nWhere access to a Game depends on third-party authentication, store validation, or secure session management, we process identifiers, authentication confirmations, tokens, technical session data, and related metadata to confirm that you are authorized to access the relevant Game environment and to keep the Game secure.\n\n3.4. To process in-game purchases, rewards, and entitlements\n\nWe process personal data to validate purchases, assign purchased items or currency, manage subscriptions where applicable, investigate chargebacks or fraud, reconcile reward distributions, and maintain the integrity of monetization systems. This may include store transaction IDs, entitlement status, purchase timestamps, and similar data received from app stores or payment partners.\n\n3.5. To communicate with you\n\nWe process personal data to send you operational and administrative communications related to the Games, including support responses, security alerts, important technical notices, and notices regarding changes to terms, policies, or core Game functionality.\n\n3.6. To provide customer support and resolve disputes\n\nWe use your contact data, support history, gameplay context, logs, screenshots, and related information to answer questions, investigate technical issues, resolve disputes, review moderation decisions, and address claims or complaints. As detailed in Section 2.4, certain support, account-authentication, recovery, or purchase-related assistance functions may also be carried out on our behalf by third-party service providers, where necessary to provide support in connection with the Games. \n\n3.7. To maintain safety, security, and fair play\n\nWe process personal data to secure the Games, detect and investigate fraud, botting, abuse, cheating, unauthorized access, exploit attempts, payment abuse, account compromise, and violations of our rules.\n\n3.8. To moderate communities and enforce our rules\n\nWe process personal data to administer our End User License Agreement (available at: https://pixeltechnologies.io/eula). This includes handling player in-game reports, applying moderation measures (for example, in-game chat moderation), suspending or restricting access to the Games or their features, recording sanctions, investigating repeat abuse, and protecting players and the Games from harmful conduct, including, where necessary, cooperation with the publisher, rightsholder, or operator of the global version of the Game for shared (cross-play) enforcement.\n\n3.9. To show advertising and measure marketing performance\n\nWhere a Game includes advertising or user-acquisition measurement, we may process advertising identifiers, campaign data, device information, ad impressions, ad-click events, attribution data, and related analytics to deliver contextual or personalized ads where permitted, cap frequency, measure campaign effectiveness, prevent ad fraud, and understand user acquisition performance. Where consent is required for personalized advertising or device-level tracking, we will rely on that consent and your platform-level privacy choices.\n\n3.10. To comply with the laws and protect our rights\n\nWe may process personal data where necessary to comply with legal, regulatory, tax, accounting, anti-fraud, or law-enforcement obligations; to respond to valid legal requests; to protect our rights, systems, business, personnel, and players; and to establish, exercise, or defend legal claims.\n\nIf you choose not to provide certain data that is necessary for the relevant Game or feature, we may be unable to provide some or all features of the Game, process purchases, respond fully to support requests, or maintain your progress and account-linked functionality.\n\n4. MOBILE IDENTIFIERS, SDKs, LOCAL STORAGE, AND SIMILAR TECHNOLOGIES\n\nSome of our Games are mobile products. In such a case, our data collection commonly relies on mobile SDKs, local storage, server-side telemetry, device identifiers, and similar technologies rather than traditional website cookies alone.\n\nThese technologies may be used to:\n•\tremember your settings and language preferences; \n•\tkeep you signed in where supported; \n•\tsave progress and Game state; \n•\tmeasure installations, sessions, events, ad performance, and campaign attribution; \n•\tprevent fraud and protect the security of the Games; and \n•\tpersonalize content or advertising where permitted by law and by your settings. \n\nYou may also be able to limit certain forms of tracking through your device or platform settings, including advertising and app-tracking controls offered by Apple, Google, Huawei, or your device manufacturer. If you opt out of personalized advertising, you may still see advertisements, but they may be more general or contextual.\n\n5. WHEN WE SHARE PERSONAL DATA\n\nWe do not sell your personal data. We share personal data only where there is a legitimate operational, contractual, legal, or security reason to do so, and only to the extent necessary.\n\n5.1. With other users\n\nSome information is visible to other players by design of the multiplayer and social features of the Games. Depending on the Game and your settings, other users may see your nickname, avatar, profile content, guild or team affiliation, achievements, status, selected gameplay statistics, leaderboard position, and content you voluntarily make available through in-game interactions. If you participate in chats, teams, guilds, events, or similar features, your information may be shared as part of that interaction.\n\n5.2. With app stores, account providers, and distribution partners\n\nWe may share limited information with app stores, authentication partners, distributors, and related service providers to enable login, entitlement management, fraud prevention, customer support, event administration, or account synchronization. Where those providers manage your primary account or credentials, they process related data under their own policies.\n\n5.3. With service providers and processors\n\nWe may engage third-party vendors, contractors, and service providers that process personal data on our behalf for functions such as cloud hosting, game backend services, analytics, crash reporting, customer support systems, communications delivery, ad mediation, fraud prevention, anti-cheat support, data storage, and other business operations. These parties receive only the data needed to perform their functions and are required by contract to protect the data, maintain confidentiality, and process it only on our documented instructions where applicable.\n\n5.4. With payment and commerce partners\n\nWe may share or receive data with or from app stores, payment processors, commerce partners, and financial service providers as necessary to validate transactions, prevent fraud, manage refunds or disputes, and comply with legal obligations. We typically do not store full payment-card details where those details are entered into third-party payment environments.\n\n5.5. With advertising, attribution, and analytics partners\n\nWhere relevant to a Game, we may share certain technical and advertising-related data with advertising, attribution, mediation, and analytics partners in order to display ads, attribute installs, measure campaign performance, prevent fraud, and improve Game delivery. Where required by law, such sharing will be subject to consent or platform-level authorization mechanisms.\n\n5.6. For legal reasons, compliance, and protection\n\n",
    "We may disclose personal data to courts, regulators, law-enforcement authorities, government bodies, professional advisers, or other third parties where required by law, where necessary to respond to a valid legal request, where necessary to protect the rights or safety of Pixel, our users, or the public, or where necessary to investigate fraud, abuse, or security incidents.\n\n5.7. In connection with corporate transactions\n\nIf we are involved in a merger, acquisition, financing, asset sale, reorganization, insolvency proceeding, or similar transaction, personal data may be disclosed to relevant counterparties, advisers, and successors subject to appropriate confidentiality and lawful-processing requirements.\n\n6. INTERNATIONAL AND CROSS-BORDER TRANSFERS\n\nThe Games are operated from the United Arab Emirates. To provide the Games, including the cross-play and shared game functionality described in Section 3.2, we may transfer personal data to, access it from, or allow it to be processed in countries outside your place of residence, including where our service providers, partners, publishers, infrastructure, or support operations are located.\n\nWhere we transfer personal data across borders, we will do so only where lawful, necessary for the purposes described in this Policy, and subject to appropriate safeguards under applicable law. Where applicable, this may include transfers to jurisdictions recognized as providing an adequate level of protection. Where such level of protection is not available, we may still transfer personal data where permitted under applicable law and subject to appropriate safeguards and lawful transfer mechanisms, which include, depending on circumstances of and requirements for specific transfer,  contractual data-protection commitments, processor obligations, technical and organizational security controls, internal governance measures, explicit consent where required, necessity for the performance of a contract, or another lawful basis or transfer mechanism recognized under applicable law.\n\nBy using the Games, you understand that your personal data may be transferred to and processed in jurisdictions outside your place of residence, subject to the safeguards and protections described in this Policy. Where consent is specifically required for a particular transfer or category of processing, we will obtain that consent separately.\n\n7. DATA RETENTION\n\nWe retain personal data only for as long as necessary for the purposes described in this Policy, unless a longer period is required or permitted by applicable laws.\n\nRetention periods vary depending on the nature of the data and the purpose of processing. For example:\n•\tgameplay and player-profile data may be retained while your Game profile remains active and for a reasonable period thereafter to allow restoration, dispute handling, fraud prevention, and compliance; \n•\ttransaction and financial reconciliation data may be retained for the period necessary to comply with accounting, tax, audit, anti-fraud, and legal obligations; \n•\tsupport tickets, abuse reports, moderation records, and dispute files may be retained for as long as reasonably necessary to investigate, resolve, defend, or prevent recurring issues; \n•\ttechnical logs, crash data, and security telemetry may be retained for shorter operational periods, except where a longer retention period is justified for incident analysis, fraud prevention, or legal protection; \n•\tadvertising and attribution data may be retained according to campaign, measurement, and legal requirements, subject to applicable platform rules and your choices. \n\nWhen personal data is no longer required, we will delete it, anonymize it, or securely isolate it, unless continued retention is required by law, necessary to protect our rights, or justified for another lawful purpose.\n\n8. DATA SECURITY\n\nWe are committed to protecting personal data through reasonable and appropriate technical, organizational, and administrative security measures designed to reduce the risks of unauthorized access, loss, misuse, alteration, disclosure, or destruction.\n\nOur security measures may include, as appropriate, encryption in transit, access controls, least-privilege permissions, authentication measures, secure development practices, internal policies, incident-response procedures, system monitoring, logging, backup and recovery controls, vendor due diligence, and personnel training. Access to personal data is restricted to personnel and service providers who need such access for legitimate business purposes.\n\nNo method of transmission or storage is completely secure, and therefore, we cannot guarantee absolute security. You are also responsible for helping protect your account and devices, including by maintaining the security of any credentials you control and notifying us promptly if you suspect unauthorized access.\n\nIf we become aware of a personal-data breach that requires notification under applicable law, we will take the steps required by law, including notifying competent authorities and affected individuals where legally required.\n\n9. YOUR RIGHTS IN RELATION TO YOUR PERSONAL DATA\n\nDepending on the applicable law and the circumstances of processing, you may have the following rights in relation to your personal data:\n\n9.1. Right to be informed\n\nYou may request clear information about how your personal data is processed, including the purposes of processing, categories of data, recipients, and contact details for exercising your rights.\n\n9.2. Right of access\n\nYou may request confirmation of whether we process your personal data and, where applicable, request access to or a copy of the personal data we hold about you, subject to applicable exceptions and verification requirements.\n\n9.3. Right to rectification\n\nYou may request correction of inaccurate personal data and completion of incomplete personal data. Where available, some profile or contact data may also be updated directly through in-game settings or the relevant platform account.\n\n9.4. Right to erasure\n\nYou may request deletion of your personal data in circumstances permitted by applicable law, including where the data is no longer necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, where consent has been withdrawn, and no other lawful basis applies, or where the data has been processed unlawfully. This right is not absolute and may be limited where retention is required by law or necessary to protect legal rights or Game integrity.\n\n9.5. Right to restrict processing\n\nYou may request that we restrict the processing of your personal data in certain circumstances, such as where you contest the accuracy of the data, where you believe processing is unlawful and request restriction instead of deletion, or where the data must be preserved for legal claims.\n\n9.6. Right to object or to stop certain processing\n\nWhere permitted by applicable law, you may object to certain processing activities, including direct marketing and certain processing based on our lawful interests or other permitted grounds. You may also request that we stop processing in circumstances recognized by law.\n\n9.7. Right to data portability\n\nWhere applicable, you may request to receive personal data that you have provided to us, and that we process by automated means on the basis of consent or contract, in a structured, commonly used, and machine-readable format, and you may request transmission to another controller where technically feasible and legally applicable.\n\n9.8. Right to withdraw consent\n\nWhere we rely on your consent, you may withdraw that consent at any time. Withdrawal does not affect the lawfulness of processing carried out before the withdrawal took effect.\n\n9.9. Rights in relation to automated processing\n\nYou have the right, where provided by law, not to be subject to a decision based solely on automated processing that produces legal effects concerning you or similarly significantly affects you, except where such processing is otherwise permitted by law and subject to safeguards. Where required, you may request human review, express your point of view, and contest the decision.\n\n9.10. Right to complain\n\nIf you believe your rights have been violated, you may contact us first so that we can try to resolve the issue. You may also have the right to lodge a complaint with the competent authority in the United Arab Emirates or another competent authority, as applicable.\n\n10. HOW TO EXERCISE YOUR RIGHTS\n\nTo exercise your rights or submit a privacy-related request, please contact us at:\n•\tEmail: games@pixeltechnologies.io\n•\tPostal Address: Pixel Technologies - FZCO, Dubai Silicon Oasis, IFZA Business Park, DDP, Building A1, Premises 26105-001, Dubai, United Arab Emirates\n\nWhere available, you may also use any in-game privacy, account, communication-preference, or support tools we provide.\n\nWhen you submit a request, we may ask for additional information reasonably necessary to verify your identity and confirm that you are entitled to make the request. This helps us protect users against fraudulent, abusive, or unauthorized requests.\n\nWe will review and respond to your request within the time required by applicable law. If the request is unclear, manifestly unfounded, repetitive, technically infeasible, or excessive, or if legal grounds prevent us from fulfilling all or part of the request, we may ask for clarification, limit our response as permitted by law, or refuse the request where legally justified. Where permitted by law, we may also charge a reasonable fee for excessive or repetitive requests.\n\n11. THIRD-PARTY SERVICES AND LINKS\n\nThe Games may integrate with or link to third-party services, including app stores, payment environments, social platforms, analytics providers, advertising networks, or authentication services. We do not control the privacy practices of those third parties when they act under their own policies and terms. We encourage you to review their privacy notices carefully.\n\nIn particular, where your Game access, payment, subscription, identity, ad settings, or device permissions are managed by a third party, that third party’s privacy notice will also apply to the relevant processing.\n\n12. CHANGES TO THIS POLICY\n\nWe may amend this Policy from time to time to reflect changes in our Games, technology, legal requirements, business practices, or data-processing activities. The updated version will be posted through the relevant Game, website, store listing, or other appropriate channel.\n\nWhere required by applicable law, we will provide additional notice of material changes by appropriate means, such as an in-game notice, store update notice, website posting, or direct communication.\n\n13. CONTACT US\n\nIf you have any questions, requests, or complaints regarding this Policy or our processing of your personal data, you may contact us by e-mail at: games@pixeltechnologies.io. Where available, you may also contact us through the in-game support tools or the support section of the relevant Game.\n\n14. SUPPLEMENTARY PROVISIONS FOR USERS LOCATED IN THE RUSSIAN FEDERATION \n\nIf you are located in, or reside in, the Russian Federation, certain supplementary provisions relating to the processing of your personal data may apply in addition to this Policy. Please refer to the separate supplementary privacy provisions for users located in the Russian Federation, available at: https://pixeltechnologies.io/privacy_supplementary_provisions.\n\n15. LANGUAGE VERSIONS\n\nThis Policy may be made available in languages other than English for convenience only. In the event of any inconsistency, conflict, or discrepancy between the English version and any translated version, the English version shall prevail."
  ]
}